I would like to know if anyone has been able to get NICs that use the 
em(4) driver working on OpenBSD 3.4 or 3.5. I have experienced problems 
with Intel PRO/1000XT NICs on both a XP1000 and a DS20. The XP1000 is 
currently running OBSD 3.2 since that was the last version to work 
properly on the hardware. The problems with the XP1000 are outlined at:

http://marc.theaimsgroup.com/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=107826670310083&w=2

3.5 runs fine on the DS20 provided the Intel NIC is not configured. If the 
Intel NIC is assigned an IP, the machine becomes completely unresponsive 
and must be rebooted. Below is the dmesg for the DS20. The reason the DS20 
is not running GENERIC is that GENERIC won't boot, as outlined at:

http://marc.theaimsgroup.com/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=107829056900509&w=2

The only difference between the running kernel and GENERIC is the line:
config         bsd     root on sd0a swap on sd0b

If anyone has any advice on how to get the em driver working, it would be 
greatly appreciated.

Thanks,

-- Mark Roberts



